DESCRIPTION:Join our second-to-last Working Papers Seminar with Evan Augus
 te (CUNY) and Nadège Robertson (Lakou Lapè) as we explore Lakou Tanama - 
 healing circles rooted in African and Taino worldviews that invoke ancest
 ral memory and communal care to support Haitian communities amid crisis\,
  reclaiming political agency and challenging narratives that pathologize 
 Haitian identity. Comments by Deborah Jenson (Duke University).\n\n��️ Fr
 iday\, April 17\, 2026\n⏰12:00-1:15 PM (EDT)\n��Online (Zoom - Translated
  captioning available)\n��Registration free but required\n\n�� Presenters
 :\n\nEvan Auguste (CUNY)\n\nNadège Robertson (Lakou Lapè)\n\n"Sék Lakou T
 anama: Rethreading Haitian Futures Through Tradition"\n\n��Respondent:\n\
 nDeborah Jenson (Duke University)\n\n�� Paper(s) will be circulated prior
  to the event. PLEASE REGISTER HERE: https://www.eventbrite.com/e/ancestr
 al-care-tickets-1986360330219?aff=oddtdtcreator&keep_tld=true \n\nℹ️ Tran
 slated captioning available on Zoom
DURATION:PT1H15M
