CREATED:20260413T123511Z
DESCRIPTION:In recognition of the work students have done throughout the y
 ear in the What is the Cosmos? Constellation\, we will be hosting an exhi
 bition on Friday\, April 17\, 2:00-4:00 in The Holsti-Anderson Family Ass
 embly with a reception to follow on the patio outside. Students will be c
 ontributing items\, descriptions\, and labels related to our knowledge of
  premodern literatures\, observations\, and objects\, and the installatio
 n in Perkins will be public until graduation weekend.\n\n\nAcross the fal
 l and spring semesters\, these first-year students explored the vast expa
 nse we call the cosmos. Through a multidisciplinary approach from classes
  in physics\, history\, energy\, writing\, art history\, and religious st
 udies\, students studied the shape of time and the nature of space and as
 ked whether the cosmos can be adequality represented and what is the plac
 e of the human in contemplating its purpose and harnessing its energies. 
 \n\nPlease join us as we reflect critically upon what has been imagined a
 bout worlds\, the world\, and our connection to it all.
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260417T160000
